A
flow control valve
is a specialized hydraulic valve designed to
regulate the speed of actuators
by controlling fluid flow. It combines two key components in a single body:
A
needle valve
, which will be used to
restrict flow in one direction
, controlling the actuator speed
A
check valve
, which
allows free flow in the opposite direction
, preventing unnecessary restriction when the flow direction changes
This design is especially useful in
bi-directional actuator circuits
, where different speeds are required for the forward and return strokes. For instance, a hydraulic cylinder may need to extend
slowly
while retracting
quickly
. By installing a flow control valve in the return line, fluid flow can be unrestricted in one direction, ensuring a
rapid retraction
, while controlled restriction in the opposite direction ensures a
steady and controlled extension speed
.